WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.712
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:08.479
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.779 --> 00:00:15.809
Unit twenty-six: Tourism in Cambodia. In this unit, you will talk about tourism and places that have been developed.

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:18.085
tourist attraction.

5
00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.713
tourist attraction means a place that many tourists visit.

6
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:24.988
The Royal Palace is a popular tourist attraction.

7
00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:27.957
Your turn. Say: tourist attraction.

8
00:00:30.657 --> 00:00:31.925
tourist attraction.

9
00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:34.011
heritage site.

10
00:00:34.711 --> 00:00:38.510
heritage site means a place of great historical or cultural importance.

11
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.738
Angkor Wat is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.

12
00:00:42.438 --> 00:00:44.765
Your turn. Say: heritage site.

13
00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:48.733
heritage site.

14
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.902
eco-tourism.

15
00:00:51.602 --> 00:00:55.424
eco-tourism means tourism that protects nature and helps local people.

16
00:00:55.724 --> 00:00:58.873
Eco-tourism in Mondulkiri helps protect elephants.

17
00:00:59.573 --> 00:01:02.110
Your turn. Say: eco-tourism.

18
00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:05.962
eco-tourism.

19
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:07.800
homestay.

20
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.603
homestay means staying in a local family's home as a tourist.

21
00:01:11.903 --> 00:01:14.320
We stayed in a homestay on Koh Trong island.

22
00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.046
Your turn. Say: homestay.

23
00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.723
homestay.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:22.729
tour package.

25
00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:27.774
tour package means a holiday where transport, hotel and trips are booked together.

26
00:01:28.074 --> 00:01:31.014
The tour package included three temples and a boat trip.

27
00:01:31.714 --> 00:01:34.134
Your turn. Say: tour package.

28
00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:37.963
tour package.

29
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.241
temple complex.

30
00:01:40.941 --> 00:01:44.857
temple complex means a large area with many temples and buildings.

31
00:01:45.157 --> 00:01:48.793
The Angkor temple complex covers four hundred square kilometres.

32
00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:52.227
Your turn. Say: temple complex.

33
00:01:54.927 --> 00:01:56.253
temple complex.

34
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.158
boat tour.

35
00:01:58.858 --> 00:02:01.380
boat tour means a trip on a boat to see places.

36
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.924
We took a boat tour on the Tonle Sap lake.

37
00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.939
Your turn. Say: boat tour.

38
00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:10.640
boat tour.

39
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:12.709
sunrise view.

40
00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:16.442
sunrise view means what you can see as the sun comes up.

41
00:02:16.742 --> 00:02:19.995
Thousands of visitors wait for the sunrise view at Angkor Wat.

42
00:02:20.695 --> 00:02:23.197
Your turn. Say: sunrise view.

43
00:02:25.897 --> 00:02:27.269
sunrise view.

44
00:02:28.283 --> 00:02:30.318
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:30.618 --> 00:02:33.430
Have you visited many heritage sites in Cambodia?

46
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:38.089
Yes. I've seen the sunrise view at Angkor Wat twice!

47
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:42.799
Many new roads have been built to the temples recently.

48
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:46.698
And a lot of homestays have been opened in the villages.

49
00:02:47.983 --> 00:02:51.144
Eco-tourism has been promoted in Mondulkiri too.

50
00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.658
That's great for local people. Have you ever tried a boat tour on the Tonle Sap?

51
00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.739
Grammar focus: Present perfect passive.

52
00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:06.731
Use the present perfect passive for recent changes when the action is more important than the person.

53
00:03:07.031 --> 00:03:09.355
Has or have been, plus past participle.

54
00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:12.630
For example: A new airport has been built in Siem Reap.

55
00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.764
Use it to talk about recent changes when the action matters more than who did it.

56
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.774
Now read and listen. Tourism That Helps Everyone.

57
00:03:21.074 --> 00:03:24.548
Cambodia has welcomed millions of tourists in recent years.

58
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.347
A new international airport has been built near Siem Reap.

59
00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.869
Many villages have been turned into homestay destinations.

60
00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:39.157
Eco-tourism projects have been created to protect forests and wildlife.

61
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.772
These changes have brought jobs to local people, not only to big hotels.

62
00:03:46.083 --> 00:03:48.283
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:51.267
A place of great historical importance is a blank.

64
00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:55.047
A, heritage site. B, homestay. C, tour package.

65
00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.653
The answer is A: heritage site.

66
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.906
A new road blank to the temple.

67
00:04:05.206 --> 00:04:08.708
A, has built. B, has been built. C, is building.

68
00:04:12.717 --> 00:04:14.414
The answer is B: has been built.

69
00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:18.822
The temples blank by experts from many countries.

70
00:04:19.122 --> 00:04:22.717
A, have been restored. B, have restored. C, are restore.

71
00:04:26.717 --> 00:04:29.262
The answer is A: have been restored.

72
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.214
Staying in a local family's home is a blank.

73
00:04:33.514 --> 00:04:37.144
A, boat tour. B, homestay. C, temple complex.

74
00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.103
The answer is B: homestay.

75
00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.232
According to the text, what has been built near Siem Reap?

76
00:04:47.532 --> 00:04:51.986
A, a new airport. B, a new temple. C, a new lake.

77
00:04:55.983 --> 00:04:58.412
The answer is A: a new airport.

78
00:04:59.917 --> 00:05:04.728
Now it's your turn to speak. Which place in Cambodia would you recommend to a tourist, and why?

79
00:05:10.028 --> 00:05:16.199
I'd recommend Kampot. Many guesthouses have been opened there, and the river boat tours are beautiful.

80
00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.011
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:19.017 --> 00:05:23.283
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect passive.

82
00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:27.524
Today's value is love of country. Love and take care of Cambodia.

83
00:05:27.824 --> 00:05:30.964
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

84
00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.997
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

